page in new window Search the website → Search directory → Search the Website Search the Directory Go back to Human Resources Human Resources Menu Toggle Prospective Employees Why Work at Mercer Career Opportunities Applicant Resources and Notices Benefits ↗ FAQ Current Mercer Employees Benefits and Payroll ↗ Employee Resources FLSA Information Handbooks and Policies Supervisor Toolbox Celebrating Mercerians Mercer Retiree Information Contact Us Maps and Directions Career Opportunities Skip sidebar Menu // Human Resources Prospective Employees Why Work at Mercer Career Opportunities Applicant Resources and Notices Benefits ↗ FAQ Current Mercer Employees Benefits and Payroll ↗ Employee Resources FLSA Information Handbooks and Policies Required Labor Law Posters Supervisor Toolbox Staff Recruitment Procedures Faculty Recruitment Procedures Guidelines for Hiring Independent Contractors Position Descriptions Celebrating Mercerians Mercer Retiree Information Contact Us Maps and Directions Home Prospective Employees Career Opportunities Interested in working at Mercer University? Current Mercer University Employees (including student employees) Log in to your employee Workday account to access the list of all current job opportunities. At any time, you can return to this list by typing Jobs Hub in the search bar at the top of the screen after logging in. All current employees MUST apply for any open position through their Workday account. Please note that employees in a probationary status are not eligible for consideration for current job openings outside of their department. New/Returning Users (Non-Mercer Employees) Click the Search Current Career Opportunities button below. Don’t see any current openings that are of interest to you? Sign up for Job Alerts (PDF) to be notified when positions in your interest areas are posted. Search Current Career Opportunities Mercer University’s mission is to teach, to learn, to create, to discover, to inspire, to empower and to serve. If you are drawn to opportunities where you can make a difference, then Mercer University is the place for you. Here you will find a community where your expertise will be valued, your knowledge expanded and your abilities challenged. Our tuition waiver benefits, Mercer on Mission program, and our ongoing support of the arts and athletics are just a few of the many reasons why you want to be a part of the Mercer family. Be sure to check out the Why Work at Mercer page to learn more! Diamond_4 Faculty As teachers, scholars, and researchers, our faculty have a commitment to teach, inspire, mentor and engage each individual student in his or her own path of scholarship and  discovery. While offering a breadth of programs found at much larger universities, Mercer maintains an intimate, student-focused culture more characteristic of smaller liberal arts colleges. Diamond_4 Staff As vital members of our community, our staff contribute to the university in areas such as administrative support, information technology, student support services, maintenance and law enforcement.  Regardless of the area of service, each individual contributes with their own unique talents in support of Mercer's mission. Diamond_4 Administrative Mercer's academic and administrative leadership guides the university in its' committment to excellence and innovation while challenging our community to meet and exceed high standards in teaching, learning, research, scholarship and service. Diamond_4 Mercer Engineering Research Center (MERC) As a CMMI Level 3 appraised non-profit provider of inter-disciplinary engineering and applied sciences expertise, MERC provides unique solutions to a broad range of real world problems with a strong customer support culture. Mercer University Mercer University logo displaying the words Mercer University in large white font on a dark background, all underlined in orange Contact Us 1501 Mercer University Drive Macon, GA 31207 3001 Mercer University Drive Atlanta, GA 30341 1250 East 66th Street Savannah, GA 31404 1-800-MERCER-U Quick Links Mercer Alerts Employment Libraries Canvas MyMercer Marketing Communications Information Technology Contacts Connect With Us Open Facebook page in new window Open Twitter page in new window Open Instagram page in new window © 2026 Mercer University. All rights reserved. Consumer Information Accessibility Fraud and Abuse Hotline Privacy Policy"
